+item('R2-I1', 'already fixed', 'The longer replay crossed', 'The longer replay crossed', 'Current sentence already says every batch reached 63,688-63,843 bytes under the 64,000 target, n=3.')
+item('R2-I2', 'already fixed', '| request or component', '| request or component', 'Current rows and following sentence already separate matched 23,690/4,852 from the trivial-message 2,253 probe. Experiment labels were made readable.')
+item('R2-I3', 'already fixed', 'The shared system prompt asks', 'The shared system prompt asks', 'Current sentence already distinguishes 11 non-edit turns from the one edit task, turn 35; this pass adds the narrower count and example.')
+item('R2-I4', 'already fixed', 'Round 1 saw zoom', 'Round 1 saw zoom', 'Section was already “failure modes at scale” with the round-1 5/271 and bait history. Low-effort scope added separately under R1-I3.')
+item('R2-I5', 'already fixed', 'Compaction also answered', 'Compaction also answered', 'The accurate alternative already records two distinct baits per Haiku effort and both 1517 and 5040 for Sonnet medium. The requested medium-only-one assertion contradicts retained classifications and raw markers. Extra (c) adds confirmed Sonnet low 5040.')
+item('R2-I6', 'already fixed', 'We also found a cost-sum', 'The round-1 line-writing analysis', 'Current correction already distinguishes no published line-writing USD and corrected 0.635/0.461 paired-chat totals, with 5.0/about 57 ratios; retained in the shortened note and summary.')
+item('R2-I7', 'already fixed', 'Finally, our general cost conclusion', 'The earlier break-even prediction', 'Current correction already supersedes 185-215 and 400-or-later predictions with 57/82 under stated weights; retained after relocation.')
+item('R2-I8', 'already fixed', '| request or component', '| request or component', 'Current wrapper rows already say 170 replaces about 240 and 357 confirms the prior 356 estimate, n=1 each; retained.')
+item('R2-I9', 'already fixed', '<div class="lede">', '<div class="lede">', 'Current lede already distinguishes turn-call versus total crossover and 6.019/5.995 CLI USD. This pass adds the missing Haiku one-twentieth condition and one-third counterexample.')
+item('R2-I10', 'already fixed', '- Your 98.6%', '2. Were the simulated', 'Current question already states the prefix denominator and asks for actual usage. This pass focuses it on checking the simulated shares against real usage.')
+item('R2-I11', 'already fixed', 'We said Claude Code', 'The gist says Claude Code', 'The existing correction already mentions the gist subscription lifetime and configurable default; now located beside the cost assumptions.')
+item('R2-I12', 'already fixed', 'Each cumulative column', 'Each cumulative column', 'Current table already includes turns 51-75 and current prose gives 27,300-34,442, baseline 27,839-86,316 and about 24% drift.')
+item('R2-I13', 'already fixed', 'The matched first-request comparison', 'The matched first-request comparison', 'All requested figures already frozen with n/status: stock 889,826/625,676; 23,690; baseline 32.28M/32.62M; 0.412/0.231; 17-25/232; round-1 scaled 1.84. Added the newly discussed A37 figure separately.')
+item('R2-I14', 'already fixed', 'The round-2 trial branch ended', 'The round-2 trial branch ended', 'Current sentence already pins gist revision 3c190e06, October 8, fetched October 11; full immutable hashes remain in manifest and summary.')
+item('Extra (a)', 'applied', 'In the longer replay, low-effort compaction', 'In the longer replay, low-effort compaction', 'Made the penalty sentence agree with the corrected Haiku ratio: originally 5 to 58; corrected 5 to about 57.')
+item('Extra (b)', 'applied', '- Which cache-read', '3. Does the advice', 'Audited all six questions against the gist. None asks for an already stated baseline, price, prefix denominator or tool visibility; question 3 retains only pauses and the CLI 0.05 read observation.')
+item('Extra (c)', 'applied', 'Compaction also answered', 'Compaction also answered', 'Confirmed stored sonnet-low classifications at 28+1, 28+4 and 24+8, all associated with planted message 28 and answer 5040. Cross-checked raw replies; partial corpus and source classification labels retained.')
+assert len(entries) == 40
+
+verdicts = json.loads((ROOT / '.review/round2-factcheck-full.json').read_text())
+assert [len(v['wrong']) + len(v['imprecise_or_unfair']) for v in verdicts] == [22, 15]
+out = ['# Round-2 corrections, second pass', '',
+       'Scope: all 37 items from both full reviewer verdicts, in original order, plus extras (a), (b) and (c). “Already fixed” describes the state before this pass; before/after show that current text and any editorial refinement made here. No new runs, commits, pushes or publication.', '',
+       'Evidence: saved gist, raw result rows, stored classifications and the final workflow result. Measurements and accounting were checked against raw fields; regex/file grades were not independently regraded. Reviewer recommendations that conflict with those sources use the accurate alternative and explain why.', '']
+for key, status, old, new, note in entries:
+    out += ['## ' + key, '', 'Status: ' + status + '.', '', note, '',
+            'Before:', '', '```text', old, '```', '', 'After:', '', '```text', new, '```', '']
+out += ['## Privacy and verdict-level checks', '',
+        'Status: applied. Both verdicts were read in full. The three author-read concerns are addressed in the lede and body: the 1:20 price condition with the 1:3 counterexample, questions the gist leaves open, and model attempts separated from Claude Code execution. The round-1 correction note is near the end.', '',
+        'The post and frozen study contain no email, credentials, private prompt bodies or absolute local paths. The quoted reply is synthetic. The unlisted gist is identified for this author-facing draft; nothing was published. Local source commits remain explicitly unpushed at freeze time. Review evidence remains outside the manifest artifact allowlist, which contains only summary.json. The earlier correction already removed inaccessible review-file citations from summary provenance.', '',
+        'Before: “stock with the owner\'s normal configuration”.', '',
+        'After: “stock with a normally configured install”.', '',
+        '## Frozen-study consistency', '',
+        'Status: applied. Added Sonnet-low 5040 classifications, one-third price sensitivity and compaction own-unit totals, the turn-82 200,000-token crossing, the inferred 300+ window estimate, capped-turn exclusion, prompt layout and tool-execution scope, and 667,964 UniiChat turn units at n=37. Existing correction figures and evidence labels remain. Manifest title, limitations, total-cost claim and summary hash now match.', '']
+
+POST.write_text(post)
+SUMMARY.write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + '\n')
+manifest = MANIFEST.read_text()
+manifest = manifest.replace("title: 'UniiChat through Claude Code: two rounds, a measured crossover and an untested memory claim'",
+                            "title: 'UniiChat through Claude Code: a price-dependent crossover and an untested memory benefit'")
+manifest = manifest.replace('status: depends on read price; units W2 Haiku 0.05 crossover at 82, CLI USD not reached by 112',
+                            'status: depends on read and compactor prices; W2 Haiku 0.05 crossover at 82, Haiku 1/3 and CLI USD not reached by 112')
+manifest = manifest.replace("- 'Round 2: CLI Sonnet read price is 0.05 times input versus 0.1 in the unit; USD estimates are not subscription\n  invoices.'",
+                            "- 'Round 2: fitted CLI Sonnet read price is 0.05 times input versus 0.1 in the unit; Haiku is 1/20 of Sonnet on input/write/output. These prices were not checked against a price list or invoice. At a 1/3 Haiku weight, total cost does not cross within 112 turns (7.49M versus 4.61M units).'")
+manifest = manifest.replace("- 'Round 2: E5 compactor shell commands returned successful results, all read-only or no-ops; no compactor write\n  applied. Unsuccessful tool results include permission refusals and runtime errors. Tool calls and tool-call sends\n  have different denominators.'",
+                            "- 'Round 2: Haiku-low attempted tools in 266/2383 sends; Claude Code executed 159 read-only/no-op shell commands and one file read despite an empty allow list. No compactor write applied. Execution is route behaviour; a tool-owning harness could discard attempts. No high/xhigh replay was run.'\n- 'Round 2: recall turn 105 had the same eight-request trial cap in both arms; the gist sets no zoom cap. UniiChat scored 50/54 as run and missed one of 51 outside that turn. A larger cap was not tested.'\n- 'Round 2: baseline prompt first exceeded 200000 during turn 82. Filling its reported million-token window is estimated at 300+ turns, inferred rather than measured. No smaller-window replay was run.'")
+digest = hashlib.sha256(SUMMARY.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
+manifest = re.sub(r'(  sha256: )[a-f0-9]{64}', lambda m: m.group(1) + digest, manifest)
+MANIFEST.write_text(manifest)
+out += ['## Verification', '', f'Word count by whitespace: {len(post.split())}; required range 3,500-5,200.', '',
+        f'summary.json SHA-256: `{digest}`. Manifest artifact hash: `{digest}`; equal.', '',
+        'summary.json parsed successfully with python json.load. Final shell verification is also run after these edits.', '']
+(ROOT / '.review/round2-corrections-2.md').write_text('\n'.join(out))
+print(json.dumps({'words': len(post.split()), 'review_items': len(entries)-3, 'extras': 3, 'summary_sha256': digest}, indent=2))

