.review/round2-corrections-2.md:214:To combine Sonnet turns with Haiku compactions, this table weights Haiku units at 0.05 of Sonnet units. That is the relative input, write and output price reconstructed from the CLI estimates. It keeps the gist-style read weight within each model's unit. The original E5 report used a blended coefficient as if it were a model price ratio. The final audit corrected that interpretation.
.review/round2-corrections-2.md:302:We said Claude Code's one-hour cache marks could not be changed. That was wrong. The specification notes that subscriptions mark with a one-hour lifetime; that is the default, and an environment setting changes it. E6 set `CLAUDE_CODE_PROMPT_CACHE_TTL=5m` and measured five-minute writes on the subscription route. The trial core had also hard-coded one hour on its own view mark. Our earlier account acknowledged that we had not tested a five-minute mark, then treated the untested setting as a constraint of Claude Code.
.review/round2-corrections-2.md:439:Removed E1/E3/E4/E5/E6/B2 and audit/report disputes from the post; study files retain reconciliation provenance.
