.review/round2-corrections-2.md:721:> The round-1 retry-heavy E1 USD figures have not been repaired individually. We retain them as historical reported figures with that defect recorded, rather than treating them as audited costs.
.review/round2-corrections-2.md:726:We also found a cost-sum error in the round-1 E1 analysis script. Claude Code reports cumulative USD within a process. The script summed that cumulative value on every retry row, counting earlier spend again. In the new low-effort sweep, the same naive calculation gave USD 0.412 against USD 0.231 after taking differences, over 318 sends. The defect was in the E1 analysis script and affected no E1 USD figure published here. The retained E3 whole-arm estimates move immaterially when corrected: differenced USD 0.635 and 0.461 versus the source-reported 0.640 and 0.468. The Sonnet ratio stays 5.0 times; Haiku moves from 58 times to about 57 times.
