.review/round2-corrections-2.md:868:We said Claude Code's one-hour cache marks could not be changed. That was wrong. The specification notes that subscriptions mark with a one-hour lifetime; that is the default, and an environment setting changes it. E6 set `CLAUDE_CODE_PROMPT_CACHE_TTL=5m` and measured five-minute writes on the subscription route. The trial core had also hard-coded one hour on its own view mark. Our earlier account acknowledged that we had not tested a five-minute mark, then treated the untested setting as a constraint of Claude Code.
